e79-4550-889a-59dfb70830ab","position":{"commit_sha":"c09008f178c817fbbce9bc66a92a7bf04122fbe2","position":"1788093561501394001-6fff43eb-be79-4550-889a-59dfb70830ab"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788026461495530271,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b91983d6-c3d1-4029-81c3-0ca884a88c2c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2b7f-67e3-d612-4c5b"},{"link_uuid":"472f7a42-63b3-4abf-ab31-a5846fa10301","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f27f-fb9d-3bd8-463f"},{"link_uuid":"ba23f781-71a8-4b76-881e-4b9e5a68be9c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"86b9-6a14-74cf-478d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nComplete ADR 0098 for LLM execution after the command/store cutover. Many LLM operations currently call `LLMConfig.from_env()` independently, even though `LLMRuntime`, `ProviderSession`, gate config scoping, and snapshot composition already exist.\n\nThe goal is one behavior-bearing snapshot/context per public operation, not deletion of a legitimate top-level composition convenience. Ambient compatibility may remain only at an explicitly approved boundary and must delegate to the central composer.\n\n`emit_shadow_snapshot`/`_shadow` (the RP-04 S1 diagnostic shadow ticket 3a08 retained) has SIXTEEN production call sites, not five: five in `_mcp_llm.py` (LLM), ten in `_lib_ops.py` (three LLM workflow ops — `run_workflow`/`get_workflow_status`/`get_workflow_result` — plus seven NON-LLM bridge/reconciler-mapping call sites covering the eight public bridge ops, since `bridge_preview`/`bridge_sync` share one call inside `_bridge_run`), and one in `_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py::_emit_operation_shadow`. Deleting the shared functions (AC5) requires ALL sixteen migrated first — see Scope. Four existing test modules assert on the retired symbols directly (`tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py`, `tests/unit/test_single_definition_helpers.py`, `tests/scripts/test_residual_drain_seam_clean_heldout.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_operation_snapshot_surfaces.py`) and are updated in lockstep — see Scope.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Derive a focused LLM config projection from the existing snapshot/schema/provenance; pair it with existing non-serializable `LLMRuntime`.\n- Thread that context through gate/workflow/runner entry points so subcalls inherit policy rather than re-resolving it.\n- Preserve ProviderSession/provider-native auth, budgets, cache/output/retry behavior, tracing, secret exclusions.\n- Add consumer-level metamorphic tests for multi-step runs and failure/retry paths.\n- Delete the shadow switch/function and migrated ambient-resolution branches after parity; tighten the existing ownership gate and documentation.\n\n**Call-site classification:** LLM sites bind the NEW `compose_and_bind_llm_config` — FOUR public entry points make an actual LLM call: `rebar.llm.review_code`/`verify_completion`/`review_plan`/`scan_epics_for_spec` (each reached by both the CLI and the matching `_mcp_llm.py` tool, so one binding covers CLI/MCP/Python), plus `_lib_ops.py`'s `run_workflow` (binds inside `workflow/runs.py::run()` itself — `get_workflow_status`/`get_workflow_result` are pure replay, no LLM call, no config needed). The `_mcp_llm.py` `sign_review` tool wraps `resign_plan_review`, which makes NO LLM call — EXCLUDED from the LLM binding and the parity artifact's compose-once list; like every MCP tool it still gets the general `compose_and_bind_operation_snapshot` for ticket/store reads. Non-LLM sites (`_lib_ops.py`'s seven bridge/reconciler-mapping call sites, the reconciler's `_emit_operation_shadow`) bind the EXISTING general `compose_and_bind_operation_snapshot` (ticket 3a08's composer, no new machinery), completing the cutover 3a08 deferred here; the `_mcp_llm.py` registrar is also wrapped with this same general binding (closing 3a08's noted 'pending ec44' gap), independent of the LLM-specific composer. Once no production caller remains, `emit_shadow_snapshot`/`_shadow`/`shadow_enabled`/`SHADOW_ENV` are deleted, and any re-export (`rebar/config.py`) removed with them.\n\n**AC3 fail-fast vs. the general snapshot's fail-open (deliberately DIFFERENT contracts):** `compose_and_bind_operation_snapshot`, reused verbatim for the non-LLM sites, keeps its established fail-open swallow — unchanged, already-accepted 3a08 behavior for CLI/store ops. The NEW `compose_and_bind_llm_config` for LLM sites does NOT inherit that swallow: `LLMConfig.from_env()`'s `ConfigError`/credential/provider-resolution failures propagate uncaught, so an LLM op with unresolvable auth fails before any external call (AC3) rather than degrading to unbound ambient resolution. The two composers are independent; only the LLM one is held to AC3's fail-fast bar.\n\n**Parity-verification artifact:** `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_llm_config_authoritative_binding.py` (new, mirrors 3a08's `test_operation_snapshot_authoritative_binding.py`) asserts through production entry points: (1) compose-once/reentrancy — `review_code`/`verify_completion`/`review_plan`/`scan_epics_for_spec`/`run_workflow` (NOT `resign_plan_review`, see classification above) each bind exactly one `LLMConfig`, nested gate/workflow steps observe the identical (`is`) instance; (2) value parity vs. pre-cutover `LLMConfig.from_env()`; (3) the metamorphic/failure-edge/secret-boundary cases below. This file, plus the existing focused suites passing unchanged, is the \"parity\" gate AC5's deletion is conditioned on.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_operation_config.py` — remove diagnostic shadow machinery (`emit_shadow_snapshot`, `_shadow`, `shadow_enabled`, `SHADOW_ENV`) after every call site below is migrated.\n- `src/rebar/llm/` (incl. `config.py`'s `gate_config`/`resolve_gate_config` and a new LLM config-binding module) plus `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`.\n- `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py` — migrate all ten `_shadow(...)` sites: three LLM workflow ops (`run_workflow` delegates to `workflow/runs.py::run()`'s own binding; the two replay-only ops need no binding), seven non-LLM bridge/reconciler-mapping sites (covering eight public bridge ops) onto the existing general snapshot binding.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py` — migrate its one `emit_shadow_snapshot(surface=\"reconciler\")` site onto the existing general snapshot binding.\n- `src/rebar/config.py` — remove any `SHADOW_ENV`/`shadow_enabled` re-export once the underlying symbols are deleted.\n- Focused LLM/provider/cache/fallback/workflow tests and cross-surface contract tests, incl. the new `test_llm_config_authoritative_binding.py` parity/metamorphic/failure-edge suite, and the four existing test modules named above.\n- `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`, `docs/config.md`, and `docs/architecture.md`.\n\n## Testing\n\nHappy path: CLI, MCP, Python multi-step gates use one snapshot, preserving current provider/cache/retry/output behavior. Metamorphic edge: mutate every behavior-bearing LLM setting after composition; the active run stays stable, the next observes it. Failure edges cover missing/conflicting auth, retries, fallback, workflow subcalls, secret/non-secret boundary leakage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Each public CLI, MCP, and Python LLM/gate operation composes one snapshot/context; every subcall and workflow step receives its projection/runtime without rereading environment/files/CWD.\n- [x] Mutating model/provider class, timeout, retry, cache, headers, tracing, or repository settings after composition cannot change an in-progress multi-step run; the next operation observes the mutation.\n- [x] Explicit supplied config/snapshot stays authoritative, and missing/conflicting decision-bearing provider/auth composition fails before an external call without anonymous/cross-provider fallback.\n- [x] `LLMRuntime` and `ProviderSession` remain the live-auth and provider-resource owners; no secret/live capability enters snapshot bytes, fingerprints, repr, logs, exceptions, or schemas.\n- [x] `emit_shadow_snapshot`, its migration switch, diagnostic-only production call sites (LLM AND non-LLM — see Scope), and migrated below-boundary `LLMConfig.from_env` branches are deleted. Any retained `from_env` public composition wrapper delegates once to the central composer and is structurally allowlisted by exact symbol/rationale.\n- [x] The ownership gate fails on synthetic direct/aliased ambient reloads and carries zero post-cutover legacy exceptions.\n- [x] Consumer-level metamorphic tests plus focused LLM/provider/cache/fallback/workflow suites, default suite, lint, typecheck, complexity, and module-size gates pass; docs and ADR 0098 describe the authoritative state rather than shadow mode.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_operation_config.py","reason":"Retire diagnostic shadow composition."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/","reason":"Snapshot-derived LLM config and context threading."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/","reason":"LLM CLI operation composition."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"LLM MCP operation composition."},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"General snapshot binding for the MCP tool registrar (closes 3a08's pending-ec44 gap)."},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_ops.py","reason":"Migrate LLM workflow ops and non-LLM bridge/reconciler-mapping sites off the shadow diagnostic onto the compose-once snapshot/config binders."},{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"Remove SHADOW_ENV/shadow_enabled re-export now that the underlying symbols are deleted."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py","reason":"Migrate the reconciler's emit_shadow_snapshot call site onto the general snapshot binding."},{"path":"tests/unit/","reason":"LLM metamorphic, provider, cache, fallback, and workflow coverage."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/","reason":"Cross-surface authoritative LLM configuration tests."},{"path":"tests/scripts/","reason":"Update residual-drain-seam coverage for the retired shadow symbols."},{"path":"scripts/check_config_ownership.py","reason":"No below-boundary ambient LLM resolution."},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"Authoritative OperationSnapshot state."},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"Remove shadow-mode guidance and document boundary semantics."},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Regenerated registry after removing the deleted shadow-env read."},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"Describe the completed LLM-surface authoritative binding; retire stale shadow-machinery-is-live language."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","eb64-844b-ab7a-4915"],["relates_to","2b7f-67e3-d612-4c5b"],["relates_to","86b9-6a14-74cf-478d"],["relates_to","f27f-fb9d-3bd8-463f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","parent_status_uuid":"c47dab60-05e6-4201-aeac-7faa78d2c1b3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["configuration","llm","cutover"],"ticket_id":"ec44-b572-1067-4c52","ticket_type":"story","title":"Make OperationSnapshot authoritative for LLM operations and retire shadow resolution","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ddfbab76-02f9-4b67-8c8e-3f115f8d4985","66e50bfd-1210-4b84-8d88-607694932790","aca06e6e-9c55-46f9-b908-5f5d6a096009","3125a195-6a16-4169-b07c-3105ec7e8758","8e625d4d-8cbf-4669-a7a7-fff274bc2894","0d9f5b26-d0de-4be5-9e91-0a5c19b0c9a1","b91983d6-c3d1-4029-81c3-0ca884a88c2c","472f7a42-63b3-4abf-ab31-a5846fa10301","ba23f